<title>USA: Schnitzer may buy back up to 500,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Schnitzer may buy back up to 500,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schnitzer Steel Industries Inc said Friday that it may, from time to time, repurchase up to 500,000 shares of its Class A common stock through the open market.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe the company's stock is undervalued at current levels and is not reflective of the strength of the company and its competitive position in the marketplace,&quot; a company statement said.</p>
<p>Schnitzer's shares closed Friday down 3/16 at 23-1/16.</p>
<p>The company operates one of the largest scrap recycling businesses in the Western United States.</p>
</text>
